## SETTLED PREMISES (inlined; say if you cannot verify one)
1. The shipped edit changed one comparison, `if (depth == 4)` -> `if (depth == 32)`, where `depth`
   is a count of BITS (`8 << field`, so 8/16/32/64). The old form was unreachable. The guarded body
   is exactly two statements: `src_mode |= DE_MODE_TYPE_RGBA; dst_mode |= DE_MODE_TYPE_RGBA;`.
2. The edited comparison sits in ONE block served by THREE case labels of `switch (dst_tlb)`:
   `MTE_TLB_A`, `MTE_TLB_B`, `MTE_TLB_C`. The comparison and its body do NOT read `dst_tlb`.
3. The shipped detector's rows ALL drive `dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A` (plus one `fill b top` row that
   pins packing on TLB_B). Therefore the mutant `if (depth == 32 && dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A)` is
   PREDICTED to escape it (a build is scheduled; treat it as predicted, not measured).
4. The carrier's clause-(d) DEPENDS-ON enumeration reads, verbatim:
   > DEPENDS ON enumerates exactly two things: (1) the predicates DOMINATING the diff's edited
   > lines, walked up only to the ENCLOSING FUNCTION BOUNDARY -- never into callees or callers;
   > and (2) for operand-swap forms, swaps drawn ONLY from fields the guarded BODY reads.
5. The pass-10 joint-cells ruling reads, verbatim:
   > DEPENDS-ON enumerates JOINT cells over the guard's operands and the body-read lvalues EXACTLY
   > WHEN THE GUARDED BODY'S OWN CODE DISTINGUISHES THEM. For each lvalue take the PARTITION the
   > body's own tests induce; the enumerated cells are the CROSS-PRODUCT of those partitions.
   and, of the pcc2 TxICR case, "the label x p1 x p2 x IEN product" was closed with "the dispatch
   axes as full axes".
6. The pass-11 bound reads, verbatim:
   > The rule ENUMERATES joint cells wherever the body distinguishes them; the FLOOR -- the cells
   > a row is OWED for -- is the cross-product of the guard's dominating predicates with the
   > device-STATE lvalues the fix's own repair path reads that are JOINTLY REACHABLE through its
   > own data flow. ... A filter may reject or discharge a cell but may demand a new row only for
   > a floor cell.
7. The SIBLING PARITY pre-table row reads: "at a block that serves TWO case labels the siblings
   are the LABELS".

