 succeeded in 4133ms:
commit 2956c7e837cc5020315d6a90920860faf60c534e
Author:     indigoidk <indigoidk@users.noreply.github.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Sep 7 18:58:11 2026 -0500
Commit:     indigoidk <indigoidk@users.noreply.github.com>
CommitDate: Mon Sep 7 18:58:11 2026 -0500

    #509 sgimtedepth4dead: `depth == 4' is unreachable, so tiled MTE always took CI
    
    dev_sgi_re.c, do_mte_transfer(): `depth' is a count of BITS (8 << a two-bit field,
    so 8/16/32/64 only) and 4 is the corresponding BYTE count.  Both
    `|= DE_MODE_TYPE_RGBA' assignments were therefore dead, every tiled transfer took
    the CI arm, and at 32bpp CI assigns buf[0] alone while memory_rw copies four --
    publishing three bytes of host stack into guest memory.  One token: `depth == 32'.
    
      6-row witness    HEAD  5/6    witness_prefix_HEAD.raw
      14-row detector  HEAD 10/14   killtable2_20260907/M1_reinstate.raw
      14-row detector  FIX  14/14   killtable2_20260907/BASE.raw
      kill table 2     10 mutants, EVERY ONE KILLED, zero deviations from the
                       predictions pre-registered in PRETABLE.out
    
    PASS 2 REFUSED THE ROUND AND FOUND AN L2 FLOOR BREACH.  `depth >= 32' scored
    13/13 -- a clean sweep -- because nothing drove 64bpp.  Three seats found it
    independently; grok classified it clause (d), the guard's own operand with its
    bound relaxed.  Repaired in-round by `depth64 top', which now kills it alone.
    Note the shape: M6 (`>= 16') is a LARGER edit and was already killed; the
    SMALLER one escaped.
    
    Three more rows came from the panel rather than from me: `fill bot' and
    `copy 4th' close RGB-for-RGBA, which is invisible to dest[0] on either side, and
    `depth16 top' closes an over-reach that dest[0] at 8bpp cannot see.  M4 is
    reclassified clause (e), not (d): DEPENDS-ON takes predicates DOMINATING the
    edited line plus lvalues the GUARDED BODY reads, and that body -- the two `|='
    statements -- never reads MTE_MODE_COPY.
    
    THE ROUND DOES NOT CLOSE THE UNINITIALISED-BUFFER LEAK, and says so.  #509 fills
    buf[0..3] at depth 32 and so ACCIDENTALLY MASKS the 32-bit tiled cell of
    sgirebufuninit; that sibling must be kept alive on depth 16.  MTE_TLB_B/C, the
    LINEAR arm and the dst_tlb default arm are disclosed, not rowed.
    
    Also in this commit:
    
    L4 -- five `negate=True' rows across three witnesses went GREEN on a
    NON-OBSERVATION ("absent", "died", 0x0), found by a codex probe-helper audit.
    Repaired to positive form and measured in BOTH directions against /bin/true:
    pre-repair all five score ok (4/10, 3/7, 2/6), repaired all five FAIL (2/10,
    1/7, 1/6), and the real-build scores did not move (10/10, 7/7, 6/6).  The
    detectors never escaped -- an equality sibling reds on every one of those states
    -- so what was wrong was each row's own NOTE.
    
    The RETROSPECTIVE PASS 2 on 7a41b3f, which precommit section F refused the next
    commit for want of.  Six seats; verdict RATIFY ALL FOUR, do not revert.  It
    found three wrong records, corrected here in place:
    
      * #508's "every walked access resolved to the page's first bytes" OVERCLAIMS.
        The Alpha fast path recomputes `addr & 8191' itself, so a cache HIT reads
        correctly; the corruption is the SLOW-PATH FILL.  Corrected at four sites.
      * alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py claimed masks 0x3fff and 0x7fff are equivalent
        inside an 8 KB page so no row kills them.  ARITHMETICALLY FALSE: the premise
        is about an offset, the expression masks the full virtual address, and
        `walk vpn' drives vaddr 0x3008 where both give 0x3008 against the correct
        0x1008.  walk vpn kills all four lesser masks, not three.
      * #507's "three lines up" is four (278 vs 282), derived by a seat from the
        hunk header alone.
    
    Filed: alphapteprot (every successfully walked Alpha page returns 2, which
    memory_rw caches WRITABLE, with flags and all seven protection bits untested),
    mtesrcdup, negrowclass, probeneedleterm, gdrommappedvacuous, sessionechosat,
    sessionrefused, printedvariants, armbfxwidth32, dec21143deadclamp, shiftubcensus.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

