317: #  put bg>>24 at dest[0]" -- NOT "RGBA specifically ran".  `fill bot' is the row that separates
318: #  those two.  A flag whose name overclaims is how a future reader builds on a fact nobody has.
319: #  The pass-2 glm seat derived this from the packet alone -- under a per-row reading the copy
320: #  rows could never pass, since their own dest[0] is 0x1a and not 0x11, so BASE 13/13 would be
321: #  impossible.  It is a FIX-PRESENCE indicator: it says the repaired branch fired at all, which
322: #  is the precondition for any tail byte being defined.  A copy row therefore reports n/a when
323: #  the FILL was CI, even if the copy path itself was fine -- see the message text below.
324: #
325: #  *** TWO MEASURED LIMITS OF THIS PROXY, both from the pass-2 grok seat, recorded rather than
