The rule turns on two separate points: the switch dispatch dominates the comparison, while the full-axis and sibling-label rulings determine whether A/B/C need separate witnesses. The absence of a body read does not remove that dispatch route under clause (1). I also checked commit 2956c7e: its detector drives exactly five of the earlier 72 input combinations, all with source A and destination A.
codex
**VERDICT: I withdraw the 72-combination rationale. Under the quoted rulings, A/B/C are separate dispatch floor cells; the actual #509 detector lacks B and C comparison witnesses. The proposed escape remains predicted, not measured.**

Arguing against my pass-1 position first: 72 counted admitted inputs, without establishing that the rule requires those distinctions. The source-selector acceptance check does not distinguish A from B from C within its accepted region. The fill/copy test occurs later. The two guarded assignments do not test those choices. Moreover, three labels sharing a block do not constitute three individually dominating predicates: the common entry condition is membership in A/B/C. Thus ordinary control-flow analysis alone does not justify my enumeration. My earlier claim that `fill b top` covered B was also wrong for the named detector.

For **Q1**, yes: the switch dispatch dominates the edited comparison. Each execution reaching that comparison passes through this dispatch, within the enclosing function. The individual label equalities do **not** each dominate it.

The carrier sentence I rely on is premise 4:

> DEPENDS ON enumerates exactly two things: (1) the predicates DOMINATING the diff's edited lines, walked up only to the ENCLOSING FUNCTION BOUNDARY -- never into callees or callers; and (2) for operand-swap forms, swaps drawn ONLY from fields the guarded BODY reads.

Clause (1) admits the dispatch independently of clause (2). Premise 6 then describes the floor as the “cross-product of the guard's dominating predicates with the device-STATE lvalues the fix's own repair path reads”. The body-read qualification restricts the state-lvalue factor; it does not require a dominating dispatch selector also to qualify through that factor.

The **label granularity** comes from the additional stipulated rulings: “the dispatch axes as full axes” and “the siblings are the LABELS”. Read together, these preserve A, B and C separately despite their common target block. The body-induced partition restriction prevents inventing additional state distinctions; it does not erase the independently admitted dispatch axis. Without those label-granularity rulings, dominance alone would establish only the combined A/B/C entry condition.

This separates M4 from B/C: M4 qualifies through neither route; the destination dispatch qualifies through clause (1). Its absence from the two assignments’ direct reads does not defeat that qualification.

For **Q2**, the disputed label obligation is **three comparison witnesses**: A × the 32-bit fill’s repair-sensitive leading output byte; B × that same observable; C × that same observable. This is the existing `fill top` channel, which distinguishes whether the comparison’s type-setting repair took effect. It does not, by itself, establish every property of RGBA packing.

A is covered; **two witnesses remain owed**, for B and C. These counts concern the disputed dispatch obligation, not the detector’s entire collection of controls and other mutation checks. Reaching B or C through a helper does not change the asserted property into array-selection correctness: the assertion must still observe the repaired comparison’s effect.

Yes, this warrants a follow-up detector correction and correction of the clause-(e) classification. The missing floor coverage is established from the row definitions; the A-only mutant’s escape remains a prediction pending the scheduled build. The pcc2 label axis receives the same treatment here; its additional p1/p2/IEN factors provide no justification for importing my extra source-selector and fill/copy factors into #509.

For **Q3**, the consequence is conditional but real: where one of \(n\) reachable labels has the required comparison witness and the others have neither coverage nor a valid discharge, there are \(n-1\) missing label obligations for that observable. Merely finding a multi-label block does not establish a detector’s deficit; existing coverage, reachability and discharges still need checking.

The future-round discriminator is: **Treat an in-function dispatch dominating the edit as a full label axis, then require witnesses for its jointly reachable floor cells that existing coverage or a valid discharge does not close.**

For **Q4**, taking pair order as source then destination, the named detector drives exactly **five of the 72 combinations**: AA/fill/8, AA/fill/16, AA/fill/32, AA/fill/64 and AA/copy/32. Multiple assertions observe the same combination; `live`, `devsig` and `paint ok` do not exercise the edited comparison.

There is **no `fill b top` row** in either the current named probe or its version at commit 2956c7e. Consequently, premise 3’s parenthetical cannot be verified and is contradicted by those files. A genuine B/32-bit MTE row asserting the same repair-sensitive leading-byte property would also contradict the predicted escape: it would catch the A-only restriction.

My 72 counted the **input space**, not the partitions distinguished by the guarded body. The unexercised 67 combinations therefore are not 67 demonstrated floor omissions. The B/C omissions follow from the separate dispatch rule.

For the evidence basis, I read [do_mte_transfer](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1433), the [probe’s mode construction and row list](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_mte_fill_probe.py:219), and the relevant [header constants](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/crmfbreg.h:256), plus the source diff and probe snapshot at 2956c7e. These verify premises 1–2 and the corrected version of premise 3. I took premises 4–7 and the panel history from your packet; I did not independently authenticate the full carrier or pcc2 adjudication. I ran no detector or mutant build.
